1
00:01:13,081 --> 00:01:15,878
Frost fills the sky over
Ten Mile Lake

2
00:01:17,018 --> 00:01:19,816
Silken threads anxicus of
youth.

3
00:01:21,022 --> 00:01:23,616
Looking at the moon and
feeling lonely.

4
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:26,950
Envious of love, not of
imortality.

5
00:01:27,762 --> 00:01:31,254
This pointing will remind
you of me.

6
00:01:32,267 --> 00:01:34,565
Sian's grave?!

7
00:01:36,071 --> 00:01:38,062
Sian died long ago.

8
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:40,334
She's ghost?!

9
00:01:42,877 --> 00:01:46,973
Yes! l'm a ghost but l bring
mortals no harm.

10
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:49,544
l died far away from my home

11
00:01:49,684 --> 00:01:51,675
An evil spirit took by corpse and
won't let me rest in peace.

12
00:01:52,554 --> 00:01:57,150
lf you want to save me, move
my bones away from here.

13
00:01:57,525 --> 00:01:58,924
Then it will be possible for
me tobe reincarnated.

14
00:02:00,528 --> 00:02:01,517
Sian!

15
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:03,122
l will save you.

16
00:02:09,037 --> 00:02:10,129
Sian!

17
00:02:10,572 --> 00:02:11,869
Ning!

18
00:02:20,382 --> 00:02:21,679
Let them go, please.

19
00:02:25,253 --> 00:02:27,448
The Diamond Sutra!

20
00:02:34,129 --> 00:02:35,926
We've escaped!
Sian, we're safe!

21
00:02:36,898 --> 00:02:37,990
Dawn is breaking.

22
00:02:38,967 --> 00:02:40,958
Sian, hide in the tower of ashes.

23
00:02:41,736 --> 00:02:44,227
lf the sun's rays shine on
you, you'll never be reincarnated.

24
00:02:45,974 --> 00:02:47,669
Ning, good-bye forever!

25
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:05,022
l hope that Sian will be reincarnated.

26
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:07,758
l must return to the Orchid
Buddhist Monastery.

27
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:11,528
lf you need me, you can find
me there. Take care!

28
00:03:22,143 --> 00:03:25,635
Looking for the way,
the way of freedom.

29
00:03:25,814 --> 00:03:29,807
Sea and mountains,
l have traversed countless times.

30
00:03:30,185 --> 00:03:32,881
A thousand paths,

31
00:03:33,488 --> 00:03:37,083
all leading to my homeland.

32
00:03:37,959 --> 00:03:40,951
The endless verdent mountains,

33
00:03:41,196 --> 00:03:44,893
The mountains everywhere,
in howling wind and driving rain.

34
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:48,298
The path of the ancient garden.

35
00:03:48,903 --> 00:03:52,498
Why does it never end?

36
00:03:56,511 --> 00:04:00,208
The way of the Tao, the way of freedom.

37
00:04:00,348 --> 00:04:04,341
Devils and demons always
pronounce themselves good.

38
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:07,620
The anger of youth

39
00:04:08,056 --> 00:04:11,651
Weeping ghosts and angry spritis,

40
00:04:12,394 --> 00:04:15,488
Times gone-by,

41
00:04:15,697 --> 00:04:19,690
Why was there such a sea of blood?

42
00:04:20,067 --> 00:04:22,866
The path of the ancient garden

43
00:04:23,371 --> 00:04:27,068
Why can one never return on it?

44
00:04:32,914 --> 00:04:34,404
Who is that young man?

45
00:04:34,516 --> 00:04:36,814
He's the poor schoolar who
lived 2 blocks away.

46
00:04:37,051 --> 00:04:39,952
Things have changed since he
was last here.

47
00:04:55,437 --> 00:04:58,235
Wasn't he that shop's bill
collector?

48
00:04:59,174 --> 00:05:01,972
He doesn't even know it went
out of business long ago!

49
00:05:14,189 --> 00:05:15,486
Welcome! Welcome!

50
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,352
The bill collector's here.

51
00:05:48,456 --> 00:05:49,650
How much money did you collect?

52
00:05:50,859 --> 00:05:51,951
We're here to catch escaped convicts.

53
00:05:52,193 --> 00:05:53,285
lt's the police! Run!

54
00:05:53,428 --> 00:05:54,326
Pursue them!

55
00:05:58,132 --> 00:05:59,429
You're Bing Chow?!

56
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:02,365
You've made a mistake.
He has a beard and l don't!

57
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:03,559
You shaved it off!

58
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:04,727
Take him back and collect the reward.

59
00:06:05,106 --> 00:06:06,004
Get in!

60
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:08,770
l haven't committed any crime!

61
00:06:09,143 --> 00:06:11,236
Let me got. l've been
wrongly accused!

62
00:06:11,479 --> 00:06:13,379
Let me got l've been
wrongly accused!

63
00:06:13,982 --> 00:06:16,177
You're made a mistake.
l'm not Bing Chow!

64
00:06:16,384 --> 00:06:18,181
l am wrongly accused!

65
00:06:33,401 --> 00:06:34,800
My name is Ning,
not Bing Chow.

66
00:06:35,003 --> 00:06:36,095
Old man may l ask who...

67
00:06:38,039 --> 00:06:42,237
A man just like you,
fated to being imprisoned.

68
00:06:42,577 --> 00:06:43,475
So pessimistic!

69
00:06:44,412 --> 00:06:47,313
lt's all my elders' fault,
insisting l get an education

70
00:06:47,482 --> 00:06:49,279
When l grew up, l was
learned and wrote books.

71
00:06:50,351 --> 00:06:53,149
But when l write of my travels,
l'm accused of revealting state secrets.

72
00:06:53,555 --> 00:06:55,750
When l write of history,
they say l'm satirizing the present.

73
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,718
lf l analyse milltary strategy,
they say l'm planning arebellion.

74
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:02,354
l can't even write fairy tales, for they
accuse me of promoting superstition.

75
00:07:03,197 --> 00:07:04,994
Finally, l wrote the
biography of a powerful man.

76
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:07,493
Then he was arrested,
accused of being a rebel.

77
00:07:08,369 --> 00:07:10,064
We here both sentenced to
life imprisonment.

78
00:07:10,371 --> 00:07:13,169
Wouldn't you say that prison
is my fate?

79
00:07:15,677 --> 00:07:16,769
A cockroach!

80
00:07:16,878 --> 00:07:17,867
Where?

81
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:19,678
Cockroach?!

82
00:07:23,518 --> 00:07:26,009
You're really wasteful! The
cockroaches here are of the best quality.

83
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:27,951
There are no delicacies here

84
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:30,814
After you're been here a while,
you'll even salivate ever a housefly.

85
00:07:31,859 --> 00:07:33,053
Old man, how long have you
been here?

86
00:07:33,962 --> 00:07:35,657
l was your age when
l first arrived.

87
00:07:35,930 --> 00:07:39,229
Look how l've changed!
Full of character!

88
00:07:40,101 --> 00:07:41,193
You've been here a long time

89
00:07:41,936 --> 00:07:44,234
Help! l am innocent!

90
00:07:44,339 --> 00:07:45,931
l'm not Bing Chow!
l am innocent!

91
00:07:46,074 --> 00:07:50,477
You've made a mistake.
l'm not Bing Chow!

92
00:08:20,141 --> 00:08:23,736
Another nightmate.
What did you dream this time?

93
00:08:24,245 --> 00:08:25,439
l dreamt you were haggard
and exhausted.

94
00:08:25,613 --> 00:08:27,808
Exhausted?! True, you will
soon be totally exhausted.

95
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:31,651
You have nightmares every night.
Look at the calendar.

96
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:34,286
You've been here so long and
still can't adjust.

97
00:08:34,422 --> 00:08:36,219
Soon you'll even forget that
your last name is Chow.

98
00:08:36,758 --> 00:08:37,952
Old man, my last name
isn't Chow!

99
00:08:39,027 --> 00:08:40,221
Bing Chow!

100
00:08:42,829 --> 00:08:43,922
Supper!

101
00:08:43,998 --> 00:08:45,396
OK.

102
00:08:49,837 --> 00:08:52,135
A chicken leg?!

103
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:54,240
Happy days are here again!

104
00:08:56,678 --> 00:08:58,873
Old man! There's only one
bowl. You eat first.

105
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:01,578
No, it's for you. l'd rather
eat cockroaches.

106
00:09:02,650 --> 00:09:03,742
l'll tell you something when
you've finished.

107
00:09:04,018 --> 00:09:05,417
l haven't had chicken in
a long time.

108
00:09:06,354 --> 00:09:08,254
Old man, why are you carving
my name?

109
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:12,990
All these men ate chicken legs.

110
00:09:13,194 --> 00:09:14,786
We call that chicken a
headless chicken.

111
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:17,728
After you've eaten it, they
chop off your head!

112
00:09:18,666 --> 00:09:20,065
Chop off your head?!

113
00:09:26,074 --> 00:09:30,374
Bing Chow, we have no
personel quarrel.

114
00:09:30,578 --> 00:09:32,068
Don't come back from the
greve and seek revenge on me

115
00:09:35,149 --> 00:09:38,550
They behead people at noon.
lt's now the middle of the night.

116
00:09:39,153 --> 00:09:43,146
Some official's son got in trouble,
and they're looking for a substitute.

117
00:09:43,491 --> 00:09:46,892
At night, the executioner
can't tell one from another.

118
00:09:49,497 --> 00:09:51,397
ls there no justice in the world?

119
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:57,499
ls there no reward
for being a good man?

120
00:10:00,241 --> 00:10:04,143
lt is of no concern to me.

121
00:10:15,923 --> 00:10:17,117
l was always an honest man.

122
00:10:17,792 --> 00:10:18,986
l'll give you whatever l can

123
00:10:20,495 --> 00:10:23,191
This painting was a gift
from my dearest one.

124
00:10:23,531 --> 00:10:24,623
l don't want to part with it
even in death.

125
00:10:25,466 --> 00:10:27,661
Young man, you have a good heart.

126
00:10:27,902 --> 00:10:29,893
Let me give you a present.

127
00:10:32,507 --> 00:10:33,906
You are so learned.

128
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:35,741
lt is fortunate that l die
rather than you.

129
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:37,807
You're a good man.
Such a pity you have to die.

130
00:10:37,979 --> 00:10:39,469
lt would be a pity if you
died, not me.

131
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:40,874
Anybody's death is a pity.

132
00:10:41,015 --> 00:10:42,505
You're a rare speciman.

133
00:10:42,583 --> 00:10:44,574
lf you die, your type will be extinct.

134
00:10:44,786 --> 00:10:45,878
lt's been a long time since
l set somebody free.

135
00:10:46,387 --> 00:10:48,582
This tunnel leads to the outside.

136
00:10:49,157 --> 00:10:51,057
Go out and start a new.

137
00:10:53,928 --> 00:10:55,327
Don't give me such false hopes.

138
00:10:55,730 --> 00:10:57,630
lf this is an escape route,
why didn't you escape long ago?

139
00:10:58,065 --> 00:10:59,965
lt's less troublesome for me
to write my book here.

140
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:02,396
When l finish, then l'll
escape and get it printed.

141
00:11:02,804 --> 00:11:04,396
Don't worry about me.

142
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:06,400
Always keep this bundle
with you.

143
00:11:06,774 --> 00:11:09,971
Once you're out of here,
never come back!

144
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:11,906
Get going!

145
00:11:13,014 --> 00:11:14,311
What will happen to you
after l've gone?

146
00:11:14,916 --> 00:11:16,315
They like hearing my stories

147
00:11:16,450 --> 00:11:18,042
So long as l don't get to
the story's end,

148
00:11:18,119 --> 00:11:19,211
they'll never harm me.

149
00:11:19,353 --> 00:11:20,547
But they'll accuse you of
helping me escape.

150
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:24,213
l'll say you were put to
death for somebody else 2 days ago.

151
00:11:24,425 --> 00:11:26,723
They won't dare make a fuse.

152
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,359
Go!
Take care!

153
00:11:30,765 --> 00:11:33,757
Bing Chow! The time has come

154
00:11:37,572 --> 00:11:38,561
Bing Chow!

155
00:11:38,673 --> 00:11:39,765
He's dead.

156
00:11:46,848 --> 00:11:49,942
l've escaped!

157
00:12:04,198 --> 00:12:05,495
There's even a horse here
waiting for me!

158
00:12:09,904 --> 00:12:12,600
That old man is really remarkable!

159
00:12:13,474 --> 00:12:14,964
l must repay his kindness someday.

160
00:12:20,047 --> 00:12:22,140
Hey! That's my horse!

161
00:12:22,483 --> 00:12:24,883
What a stupid horse!
Letting a stranger ride him!

162
00:12:25,586 --> 00:12:27,076
l don't even have time
to wash my hands!

163
00:12:30,925 --> 00:12:33,325
You think you're fast over land...
l'll go underground!

164
00:12:34,028 --> 00:12:35,222
Open sesame!

165
00:12:42,737 --> 00:12:44,329
l must find a place to get
out of this downpour!

166
00:12:47,875 --> 00:12:49,172
Good! A house!

167
00:12:52,413 --> 00:12:54,404
Open the door!

168
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:04,287
''Righteous Villa''...

169
00:13:13,768 --> 00:13:14,962
Anybody home?

170
00:13:20,241 --> 00:13:24,234
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8

171
00:13:24,645 --> 00:13:26,636
8 coffins! Must be the
whole family.

172
00:13:28,950 --> 00:13:32,044
l won't disturb you.
l just want to stay the night.

173
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:35,049
Don't bother to get up.
l'll take care of myself.

174
00:13:38,025 --> 00:13:42,621
l told you not to go any
trouble. Please go back!

175
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:47,624
The way you rush about in no
fixed direction!

176
00:13:48,502 --> 00:13:50,299
l had a hard time following
you underground.

177
00:13:50,504 --> 00:13:51,994
Don't you have any idea
where you're going?

178
00:13:53,474 --> 00:13:55,374
Your face looks so horrible,
you must have suffered a painful death.

179
00:13:56,010 --> 00:13:58,001
lf you'd rushed around
underground all day like me,

180
00:13:58,946 --> 00:14:00,243
you wouldn't have the energy
to come back to the surface.

181
00:14:05,586 --> 00:14:07,486
l don't know you. Why are
you following me?

182
00:14:07,588 --> 00:14:09,488
l don't know you either, so
why did you take my horse?

183
00:14:11,625 --> 00:14:12,717
That's your horse?

184
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:14,955
l thought it was the
old man's.

185
00:14:15,196 --> 00:14:17,790
Still you should have asked
before taking it.

186
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:21,299
You're alive! Sorry! lt's
all a misunderstanding.

187
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:27,100
lf there's anything l can do
to help, just let me know.

188
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:31,541
Enough of your tricks!
A good thing my reactions are so fast.

189
00:14:31,846 --> 00:14:34,041
Friend, you need a place to
stay the night.

190
00:14:34,315 --> 00:14:35,509
Here there's a roof over your head.
Might as well stay here.

191
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:38,381
How do l know what you'd
do after l fell asleep?

192
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:45,516
l knew it!

193
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,557
Let's draw up some boundaries.
l'm staying next door.

194
00:14:49,964 --> 00:14:52,262
lf you have something to say
shout it! Don't come over.

195
00:15:06,213 --> 00:15:07,612
l haven't bathed in a long time.

196
00:15:57,031 --> 00:16:01,331
The way

197
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:06,533
The spoken ''way'' is not ''way''

198
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:10,203
Of haven and earth,

199
00:16:11,312 --> 00:16:12,404
Of humang and swards

200
00:16:13,614 --> 00:16:14,706
Of evil and good,

201
00:16:14,782 --> 00:16:15,771
This way, that way, every which way

202
00:16:15,883 --> 00:16:16,679
Say that their way,

203
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:17,842
is the only way

204
00:16:17,985 --> 00:16:20,180
Bah. Tehah, hah!

205
00:16:20,421 --> 00:16:22,412
All bullshit,

206
00:16:27,428 --> 00:16:28,417
This way, that way,

207
00:16:28,596 --> 00:16:29,585
is still not the way

208
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:31,957
Ha! Ha!

209
00:16:32,166 --> 00:16:33,155
The way of flowers and tea, Ha!

210
00:16:33,267 --> 00:16:34,359
Of life and death,

211
00:16:34,468 --> 00:16:35,457
Of density and intensity,

212
00:16:35,603 --> 00:16:36,592
Of light and heat,

213
00:16:36,737 --> 00:16:37,726
Of evil spirits

214
00:16:37,905 --> 00:16:38,894
Of people committing crimes

215
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:40,734
Of bed ones in power! Ha!

216
00:16:41,275 --> 00:16:43,072
l find my own way

217
00:16:43,577 --> 00:16:47,274
l seek

218
00:16:51,085 --> 00:16:52,279
My way!

219
00:17:07,168 --> 00:17:08,362
Who is it?

220
00:17:12,373 --> 00:17:13,362
Are you a mortal?

221
00:17:17,144 --> 00:17:20,340
Hey, friend next door! Get
up! There's ghosts!

222
00:17:20,513 --> 00:17:22,310
Get up! Do you hear me?

223
00:17:22,650 --> 00:17:23,742
Hurry and get up!

224
00:17:24,551 --> 00:17:25,746
Not a sound. Maybe he left already.

225
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:47,570
What a nuisance!

226
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:04,754
Friend, there are fierce ghosts here!

227
00:18:04,825 --> 00:18:06,725
Ghosts? l'll use my maglo to
banish them!

228
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:15,830
Ghosts and goblins,
l order you to leave!

229
00:18:20,741 --> 00:18:22,936
Oh, you understand the occult!

230
00:18:24,445 --> 00:18:26,037
My nose is sensitive to
other worldly spirits...

231
00:18:26,513 --> 00:18:27,810
So why do l smell nothing now?

232
00:18:29,149 --> 00:18:29,945
Get out of the way!

233
00:18:32,186 --> 00:18:33,278
Abracadabra!

234
00:18:35,889 --> 00:18:37,880
Strange! Not even a hint of
ghostly odour!

235
00:18:38,626 --> 00:18:40,924
Abracadabra! Hocus-pocus
flash!

236
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:51,532
Abracadabra!

237
00:18:51,772 --> 00:18:57,074
Abracadabra!

238
00:18:59,146 --> 00:19:00,443
Don't come here!
Leave!

239
00:19:16,130 --> 00:19:18,325
You're not even real ghosts!
Wasting my occult talents.

240
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:19,855
Phonies?

241
00:19:34,515 --> 00:19:35,607
Want to trick me?

242
00:19:42,523 --> 00:19:43,922
A good thing you have a
waistband.

243
00:19:55,336 --> 00:19:57,031
Stay away from me!

244
00:19:58,505 --> 00:19:59,995
l'm falling...

245
00:20:01,108 --> 00:20:03,406
Stop hugging me!

246
00:20:06,113 --> 00:20:07,102
Let go!

247
00:20:07,281 --> 00:20:08,475
lf l let go, l'll fall!

248
00:20:08,682 --> 00:20:10,377
lf you don't let go, l'll...

249
00:20:39,213 --> 00:20:40,407
Sian?!

250
00:20:43,183 --> 00:20:43,979
Sian!

251
00:20:48,856 --> 00:20:53,850
Hocus-pocus heebie-jeebie!
l order you to freeze!

252
00:20:55,496 --> 00:20:56,485
Freeze!

253
00:20:57,664 --> 00:20:59,757
Freeze!

254
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:01,726
Sian, is that you?

255
00:21:03,170 --> 00:21:05,070
What kind of black magic is
that? Let them go!

256
00:21:05,572 --> 00:21:06,766
Otherwise l'll kill him.

257
00:21:07,207 --> 00:21:08,504
Oh...Freeze!

258
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:12,201
Kill him! He's no friend of mine!

259
00:21:15,682 --> 00:21:20,381
Elder Chu! Are you Elder Chu,
travelling incognito?

260
00:21:20,921 --> 00:21:22,115
Elder who?

261
00:21:22,556 --> 00:21:23,648
Your disciple is deeply sorry.

262
00:21:24,591 --> 00:21:25,683
Disciple?!

263
00:21:26,927 --> 00:21:28,121
Elder Chu?!

264
00:21:28,929 --> 00:21:32,524
Sian, it's me! Don't you
recognize me?

265
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,895
We come from a good family.
My name is Windy.

266
00:21:36,103 --> 00:21:37,297
This is my younger sister,
Moon.

267
00:21:37,871 --> 00:21:38,963
Elder Chu.

268
00:21:39,773 --> 00:21:41,365
Elder, you can save us.

269
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:43,305
My father is Lord Fu, the
ex-Minister of Rites.

270
00:21:43,577 --> 00:21:45,977
He was framed. They're now
transporting him to be executed.

271
00:21:46,113 --> 00:21:48,013
We want to attack the
transport wagon and rescue him.

272
00:21:49,283 --> 00:21:52,081
You are the learned and
brilliant Chu.

273
00:21:52,319 --> 00:21:54,514
You two are loyal imperial warriors.

274
00:21:54,888 --> 00:21:56,082
Everyone is an eminent personnage.

275
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:57,487
Now it's my turn to
introduce myself,

276
00:21:57,758 --> 00:22:01,159
l am...Spell!

277
00:22:05,666 --> 00:22:08,965
My name is Autumn,
from the Kunlun sact.

278
00:22:09,403 --> 00:22:10,893
l've read everything that
the Elder has written.

279
00:22:11,305 --> 00:22:12,704
l only use my magic to battle demons.

280
00:22:12,973 --> 00:22:14,372
l never get involved in
affairs of state.

281
00:22:15,275 --> 00:22:16,674
We pay our respects to Elder Chu.

282
00:22:18,579 --> 00:22:21,480
My name is Ning, not Chu.

283
00:22:21,849 --> 00:22:23,749
l can tell you are clever.

284
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:25,374
Clever people do not always
reveal their identities.

285
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:27,452
Anyway, in our hearts we
know who you really are.

286
00:22:28,989 --> 00:22:30,479
How can l make you believe
me?

287
00:22:31,558 --> 00:22:33,150
No need for you to say
anything. Everybody remember

288
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:35,260
From now on, Elder Chu will
be known as Ning.

289
00:22:35,529 --> 00:22:37,019
Chu is Ning.

290
00:22:37,197 --> 00:22:38,186
Yes!

291
00:22:40,133 --> 00:22:43,227
We will now take an oath.

292
00:22:43,504 --> 00:22:44,903
Whoever reveal their identities will be
chopped up into 10,000 pieces.

293
00:22:45,339 --> 00:22:46,431
Yes!

294
00:22:47,641 --> 00:22:50,542
Such an honour that you rode
my horse!

295
00:22:57,451 --> 00:23:00,249
Sian, do you remember this
painting and poem?

296
00:23:01,355 --> 00:23:04,347
Sian? Poem?

297
00:23:05,125 --> 00:23:06,820
He's reciting poetry.
Quickly, pen and paper.

298
00:23:06,994 --> 00:23:08,689
We must record what he says.
Elder is giving us a hint.

299
00:23:09,196 --> 00:23:10,595
Hurry!

300
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:14,924
Frost fills the sky over 10
Mile Lake;

301
00:23:15,335 --> 00:23:17,428
Silken threads anxious of youth.

302
00:23:17,604 --> 00:23:20,198
Looking at the moon and
feeling lonely;

303
00:23:20,474 --> 00:23:22,965
Envious of lovers, not of
immortality.

304
00:23:24,678 --> 00:23:25,872
Very profound!

305
00:23:26,647 --> 00:23:28,342
What does ''10 mile'' mean?

306
00:23:28,815 --> 00:23:31,409
10 mile!

307
00:23:32,486 --> 00:23:34,386
lt is all very deep.

308
00:23:37,391 --> 00:23:39,086
His words are too profound!

309
00:23:42,229 --> 00:23:45,323
10 Mile? That must mean 10
Mile Pavilion.

310
00:23:45,732 --> 00:23:46,926
There's a 10 Mile Pavilion
near hear.

311
00:23:48,402 --> 00:23:53,203
That's right! Sister, ''10 miles''
refers to 10 Mile Pavilion.

312
00:23:53,373 --> 00:23:54,271
lt's nearby.

313
00:23:56,310 --> 00:24:00,406
l understand. 10 Mile Pavilion
is not far from here.

314
00:24:00,681 --> 00:24:03,275
''Frost'' refers to Frost's
Descent.

315
00:24:03,684 --> 00:24:04,981
Each year has 24 climatic
periods...

316
00:24:05,319 --> 00:24:07,014
After the autumnal equinox
comes the frost...

317
00:24:07,254 --> 00:24:08,653
and today is the day of
Frost's Descent.

318
00:24:08,889 --> 00:24:11,483
Elder is telling us that father will be
transported past 10 Mile Pavilion.

319
00:24:11,692 --> 00:24:12,681
He's telling us to rescue him there.

320
00:24:12,859 --> 00:24:16,556
Elder is truly perceptive.
We can save father.

321
00:24:18,465 --> 00:24:19,762
We had it right!

322
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,130
Good.

323
00:24:22,336 --> 00:24:23,735
lt hurts!

324
00:24:24,137 --> 00:24:25,832
What's the matter? Get up!

325
00:24:26,340 --> 00:24:27,637
Reporting!

326
00:24:29,409 --> 00:24:32,310
Miss Windy! Your father will pass
the 10 Mile Pavilion tonight.

327
00:24:32,713 --> 00:24:33,907
We already know that.

328
00:24:34,815 --> 00:24:36,407
Elder is truly brilliant!

329
00:24:38,452 --> 00:24:41,148
But what about the rest of the poem?
What do those 2 stanzas mean

330
00:24:41,321 --> 00:24:42,117
3 stanzas.

331
00:24:42,289 --> 00:24:43,483
The meaning doesn't matter now.

332
00:24:43,590 --> 00:24:44,784
lnterpret it in any way you desire.

333
00:24:45,392 --> 00:24:47,292
He means that we should have
our own views...

334
00:24:47,494 --> 00:24:49,394
not just listen to what
other people say, right?

335
00:24:49,630 --> 00:24:50,927
So, should we still listen
to what Elder says?

336
00:24:51,098 --> 00:24:53,589
Not only listen, but take
notes and ponder his meaning

337
00:24:53,767 --> 00:24:55,462
We must pass his wisdom on
to future generations.

338
00:24:55,569 --> 00:24:56,467
Right!

339
00:24:56,637 --> 00:24:58,332
Time to leave!

340
00:24:58,872 --> 00:24:59,964
Good-bye.

341
00:25:00,407 --> 00:25:01,601
We're off to 10 Mile
Pavilion.

342
00:25:01,675 --> 00:25:02,767
Yes. We're off to 10 Mile
Pavilion.

343
00:25:03,410 --> 00:25:07,710
Miss Windy, please return
Sian's painting to me.

344
00:25:08,649 --> 00:25:09,741
Yes, Elder.

345
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:15,210
When you call me Sian, is
that a hint that l need a pseudonym?

346
00:25:16,023 --> 00:25:17,422
From now on, my name is Sian

347
00:25:24,297 --> 00:25:28,791
lf Sian were reincarnated,
she would now be a babe in arms.

348
00:25:33,774 --> 00:25:35,071
She's not Sian!

349
00:25:56,897 --> 00:25:57,989
What are you spying on?

350
00:25:59,499 --> 00:26:03,094
Me?...Nothing.

351
00:26:11,912 --> 00:26:13,106
What are you spying on?

352
00:26:15,482 --> 00:26:17,973
l wanted to see what you
were spying on. Time to go!

353
00:26:19,453 --> 00:26:21,751
Do you think your fiance,
Prince Ma...

354
00:26:21,988 --> 00:26:22,886
is as handsome as Elder?

355
00:26:23,390 --> 00:26:26,188
We were betrothed before birth.
How do l know what he looks like?

356
00:26:26,426 --> 00:26:28,223
ls that what people mean by fate?

357
00:26:29,629 --> 00:26:30,926
Who are you referring to?

358
00:26:31,998 --> 00:26:34,398
Oh, nobody. lt's just that l
feel so fortunate.

359
00:26:36,470 --> 00:26:38,665
Fortunate? You're frothing
at the mouth!

360
00:27:04,931 --> 00:27:05,920
Evil spirits!

361
00:27:14,007 --> 00:27:16,305
ls this a foot print or a hand print?

362
00:27:16,743 --> 00:27:17,937
We'll know when we find the
monster.

363
00:27:18,879 --> 00:27:19,777
Right!

364
00:27:24,684 --> 00:27:25,981
lt even harmad a man.

365
00:27:26,453 --> 00:27:28,546
What a pity to leave it here
Better show it to Elder.

366
00:27:29,089 --> 00:27:31,785
OK! There really are ghosts
in this place!

367
00:27:33,059 --> 00:27:33,957
What is that?

368
00:27:34,094 --> 00:27:35,891
A corpse! lt's all that
ghost's fault.

369
00:27:36,062 --> 00:27:37,461
Don't hug it. Put it down.

370
00:27:40,133 --> 00:27:41,327
How did this person die so
pitifully?

371
00:27:41,434 --> 00:27:43,834
l'd say this an evil ghost.
The odour is very strong.

372
00:27:44,604 --> 00:27:45,798
lt's back!

373
00:27:47,007 --> 00:27:48,201
ls it looking for us?

374
00:27:48,675 --> 00:27:49,573
Use your ''freeze'' magic.

375
00:27:49,743 --> 00:27:50,732
Right!

376
00:27:51,111 --> 00:27:53,807
l command you to freeze!

377
00:27:56,249 --> 00:28:01,243
Heebie-jeebie! Freeze!
That'll stop him!

378
00:28:03,857 --> 00:28:05,154
How do you do it?

379
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:07,690
When you see a ghost, shout ''freeze''.

380
00:28:08,428 --> 00:28:10,919
Like this? Freeze! ls that right?

381
00:28:11,698 --> 00:28:18,797
Oh, no! How do you lift the spell?

382
00:28:24,044 --> 00:28:25,443
l have to think of a way to
communicate with him.

383
00:28:25,579 --> 00:28:27,979
What can l do? Let's try
this...

384
00:28:28,148 --> 00:28:30,343
lf l'm right, move your eyes
up and down.

385
00:28:30,684 --> 00:28:31,878
That's right! Fantastic!

386
00:28:32,052 --> 00:28:34,646
lf l'm wrong, move them from
left to right.

387
00:28:34,921 --> 00:28:36,115
Great!

388
00:28:36,890 --> 00:28:39,882
Will a hand gesture lift
the spell?

389
00:28:51,071 --> 00:28:53,767
What? Not up and down or
left to right.

390
00:28:54,875 --> 00:28:57,070
Don't joke with me.

391
00:28:57,410 --> 00:28:59,401
lf we wait too long, that
monster will get us.

392
00:28:59,579 --> 00:29:02,878
Does lifting the spell have
to do with an acupuncture point?

393
00:29:03,450 --> 00:29:06,749
Your eyes are moving faster
than a revolving lantern!

394
00:29:07,554 --> 00:29:10,853
l understand! You're
provoking me into hitting you.

395
00:29:11,057 --> 00:29:13,958
OK. l'm going to hit you now

396
00:29:14,861 --> 00:29:15,850
Ready or not, here it comes!

397
00:29:27,407 --> 00:29:28,806
Let's get out of here!

398
00:29:32,946 --> 00:29:34,038
Come on!

399
00:29:37,317 --> 00:29:43,415
You're too heavy. l can't carry you.

400
00:29:45,625 --> 00:29:50,927
Drag it! Dragging you isn't fast
enough either.

401
00:29:51,131 --> 00:29:52,723
Better hide upstairs.

402
00:30:03,843 --> 00:30:05,538
l told you not to fool
around at a time like this.

403
00:30:09,749 --> 00:30:11,444
That monster is so tall,
it'll see us if he stand up straight.

404
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:18,282
How can l undo the spell?

405
00:30:21,494 --> 00:30:24,395
lt's safer inside. Better
hide yourself quick.

406
00:30:38,078 --> 00:30:39,170
l told you to hide inside.

407
00:30:39,279 --> 00:30:41,179
Why did you go down there,
where it's so dangerous?

408
00:31:20,086 --> 00:31:23,783
Try the ''freeze'' curse!
Freeze!

409
00:31:34,534 --> 00:31:36,126
Let's continue with out
guessing game.

410
00:31:38,371 --> 00:31:40,464
You're getting heavier and
heavier. Can't carry you much longer.

411
00:31:41,808 --> 00:31:43,105
Since that monster isn't here...

412
00:31:43,209 --> 00:31:44,801
let's try to lift the spell.

413
00:31:48,014 --> 00:31:49,413
Does it have anything to do
with this amulet?

414
00:31:51,684 --> 00:31:53,083
Yes?! What then?

415
00:31:55,588 --> 00:31:58,284
Point at me. Point at me and
the curse will be lifted.

416
00:31:58,425 --> 00:31:59,517
Point!

417
00:32:03,897 --> 00:32:09,995
How do l undo the spell?

418
00:32:24,584 --> 00:32:26,882
Freeze!

419
00:32:33,193 --> 00:32:37,596
Don't move!... Move! Move!

420
00:32:38,098 --> 00:32:39,395
Don't move!

421
00:32:41,901 --> 00:32:43,892
Why does he ''unfreeze'' so quickly,

422
00:32:44,137 --> 00:32:45,729
but you haven't moved for so long?

423
00:32:46,773 --> 00:32:51,369
Do you mean...l pointed to
this amulet...

424
00:32:52,278 --> 00:32:54,178
Then l asked you how to lift
the spell...

425
00:32:55,115 --> 00:32:57,811
And he moved! Freeze!

426
00:34:02,682 --> 00:34:04,081
l'll take care of it.
Get out of here fast!

427
00:34:05,818 --> 00:34:06,807
Finally lifted the spell!

428
00:34:08,654 --> 00:34:09,952
Get out of here!

429
00:34:10,456 --> 00:34:11,752
Abracadabra! Open up a way out!

430
00:34:14,961 --> 00:34:16,757
Abracadabra! Open up a way out!

431
00:34:20,833 --> 00:34:22,130
Out of the way! l'll take care of it!

432
00:34:31,911 --> 00:34:33,003
Abracadabra!

433
00:34:38,150 --> 00:34:39,550
Hocus pocus!

434
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:03,837
l order all ghosts to be expelled!

435
00:35:15,021 --> 00:35:16,511
Wow! lt doesn't fear my
incantations!

436
00:35:28,868 --> 00:35:29,857
lt's still moving!

437
00:35:30,737 --> 00:35:32,637
l order all ghosts to be
expelled!

438
00:35:49,422 --> 00:35:50,821
Even when it's chopped up he
can still run away!

439
00:35:51,024 --> 00:35:52,218
lt could still come back at
any time.

440
00:35:52,759 --> 00:35:54,750
Elder, get out of here.
l'll pursue it!

441
00:35:55,128 --> 00:35:55,924
Be careful!

442
00:35:56,095 --> 00:35:56,993
Earth, open up!

443
00:36:59,192 --> 00:37:01,183
Hey! Stop! Stop!

444
00:37:01,394 --> 00:37:03,692
Are you stupid? l told you to stop!

445
00:37:04,330 --> 00:37:06,321
We don't even know each other.
Why are we fighting?

446
00:37:07,467 --> 00:37:09,867
l learned magic to deal with
evil spirits.

447
00:37:09,969 --> 00:37:12,460
lf you don't stop, l'll use
my magic to ''freeze'' you.

448
00:37:13,573 --> 00:37:15,768
Why are you blocking my way?

449
00:37:16,442 --> 00:37:17,534
l was just taking a rest
after battling some ghosts,

450
00:37:17,610 --> 00:37:19,009
and you say l'm blocking
your way.

451
00:37:19,178 --> 00:37:20,975
When that monster makes a run for it
tonight, you'll be in deep trouble.

452
00:37:21,147 --> 00:37:21,943
Brother!

453
00:37:22,048 --> 00:37:23,037
Call me Master.

454
00:37:23,416 --> 00:37:24,314
Master, your skill is extraordinary.

455
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:27,146
lf you worked for the imperial court,
your future would be boundless.

456
00:37:28,421 --> 00:37:30,616
You know that l'm a
Taoist monk.

457
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:34,256
Seeking wealth and position
is for the likes of you mere mortals.

458
00:37:34,560 --> 00:37:38,553
l don't want to end up like
you...Earth, open up!

459
00:37:41,567 --> 00:37:42,864
What a pity.

460
00:37:43,035 --> 00:37:46,436
Hu, our horses' hoofs are
rigid. They won't move!

461
00:37:51,544 --> 00:37:53,239
lt must be that monk's
magic at work!

462
00:37:53,579 --> 00:37:55,774
He said there are evil
spirits. Be careful!

463
00:37:55,882 --> 00:37:56,780
Yes!

464
00:38:09,362 --> 00:38:10,556
Lord Fu!

465
00:38:11,431 --> 00:38:14,525
There's nothing l can do
about squabbles in the imperial court.

466
00:38:15,067 --> 00:38:19,163
lt's hard to tell right from wrong.
l'm just following orders.

467
00:38:19,639 --> 00:38:20,833
But don't worry.

468
00:38:22,375 --> 00:38:23,967
l'll make sure your journey is safe.

469
00:38:24,977 --> 00:38:26,171
After we get to the capital,

470
00:38:26,345 --> 00:38:29,746
whatever the emperor does to
you is not my responsibility

471
00:38:35,188 --> 00:38:36,485
Let's go!

472
00:38:47,266 --> 00:38:48,563
Where can l get something to eat?

473
00:38:54,740 --> 00:38:55,934
Please give me a bowl of
your cheapest food.

474
00:38:56,075 --> 00:38:57,167
What? The cheapest?

475
00:38:57,543 --> 00:39:01,138
Sit down! lf you're starving
don't waste your money.

476
00:39:03,916 --> 00:39:05,315
Show me your face.

477
00:39:05,685 --> 00:39:06,879
Go!

478
00:39:07,186 --> 00:39:08,380
Stand up.

479
00:39:09,255 --> 00:39:11,450
Don't lower your head.

480
00:39:12,124 --> 00:39:13,022
Go!

481
00:39:13,192 --> 00:39:14,090
Go!

482
00:39:16,696 --> 00:39:18,095
Don't run away!

483
00:39:18,197 --> 00:39:19,186
Don't move!

484
00:39:25,171 --> 00:39:26,263
Monks?

485
00:39:27,807 --> 00:39:28,899
Don't move!

486
00:39:30,009 --> 00:39:31,101
Stand still!

487
00:39:42,054 --> 00:39:43,351
Out of the way!

488
00:39:43,723 --> 00:39:44,712
Get out of the way!

489
00:40:02,375 --> 00:40:03,967
What kind of magic is this?

490
00:40:25,998 --> 00:40:27,295
lt's Windy...

491
00:40:30,469 --> 00:40:31,663
Come back!

492
00:40:32,204 --> 00:40:34,104
Hey!

493
00:40:36,943 --> 00:40:38,137
The soldiers never come to
10 Mile Pavilion last night.

494
00:40:38,311 --> 00:40:39,505
Rush back to Righteous Villa
and lie in ambush for them.

495
00:40:41,581 --> 00:40:43,879
Hey!

496
00:40:44,984 --> 00:40:46,679
Back to Righteous Villa?
lt's haunted!

497
00:40:48,087 --> 00:40:49,384
Come back!

498
00:40:56,796 --> 00:40:58,889
Elder! Elder!

499
00:41:00,733 --> 00:41:01,722
l wonder if Elder has
already gone?

500
00:41:01,968 --> 00:41:02,957
Better search for him.

501
00:41:03,102 --> 00:41:03,898
Yes!

502
00:41:07,273 --> 00:41:09,468
Do you think father's
transport has already passed by here?

503
00:41:10,109 --> 00:41:12,907
No. They're not supposed to
reach here until after dark.

504
00:41:13,346 --> 00:41:15,746
Miss Windy, the villa has
been ransacked.

505
00:41:16,482 --> 00:41:18,473
l'm sure Elder did it to
remove any traces of our presence.

506
00:41:18,651 --> 00:41:19,549
Set everything up. Prepare
to attack.

507
00:41:19,752 --> 00:41:20,548
Yes!

508
00:41:20,653 --> 00:41:21,847
Hurry up! Over there!

509
00:42:10,236 --> 00:42:11,328
Who is it?

510
00:42:11,470 --> 00:42:12,459
Who is it?

511
00:42:13,339 --> 00:42:15,330
l'm Ning.
Ning?

512
00:42:18,077 --> 00:42:19,374
Oh, it's Elder!

513
00:42:19,745 --> 00:42:20,837
This villa is haunted.

514
00:42:21,147 --> 00:42:22,239
Haunted?

515
00:42:22,348 --> 00:42:23,246
Where is Miss Windy?

516
00:42:23,349 --> 00:42:24,338
lnside.

517
00:42:25,351 --> 00:42:26,147
Ghosts?

518
00:42:26,218 --> 00:42:27,207
Real ghosts?

519
00:42:49,675 --> 00:42:50,664
Miss Windy!

520
00:42:51,777 --> 00:42:52,869
My clothes!

521
00:42:55,414 --> 00:42:56,506
Miss Windy!

522
00:42:58,451 --> 00:42:59,440
Miss Windy!

523
00:43:05,091 --> 00:43:06,388
Elder, they said you came.

524
00:43:08,227 --> 00:43:09,216
Miss Moon!

525
00:43:09,328 --> 00:43:10,226
Who are you?

526
00:43:17,002 --> 00:43:18,993
Oh, it's Elder. l recognize
your back.

527
00:43:19,572 --> 00:43:20,470
Elder...

528
00:43:23,342 --> 00:43:24,536
l...

529
00:43:29,582 --> 00:43:31,379
With your beard shaved off,
you're so, so...

530
00:43:31,951 --> 00:43:33,441
Yes.

531
00:43:34,520 --> 00:43:37,011
When my sister sees you,
she'll be so happy for me.

532
00:43:38,390 --> 00:43:39,379
Happy?!

533
00:43:39,525 --> 00:43:41,117
When you came in, did you
see my sister?

534
00:43:41,594 --> 00:43:43,494
Your sister? No. No!

535
00:43:43,896 --> 00:43:48,094
Sister! Sister! Sister!

536
00:43:51,003 --> 00:43:52,197
What are you grinning about?

537
00:43:52,605 --> 00:43:53,697
lt is improper to look.

538
00:43:58,344 --> 00:44:00,744
There are some things you
shouldn't look at.

539
00:44:01,180 --> 00:44:02,374
You're all right!

540
00:44:02,581 --> 00:44:05,175
l didn't recognize Elder
with his beard shaved off.

541
00:44:05,384 --> 00:44:06,681
Really? l must see for
myself.

542
00:44:07,386 --> 00:44:08,876
Elder, if you have something
to say, just say it.

543
00:44:09,054 --> 00:44:11,045
lt scares me when you hint
at things.

544
00:44:11,223 --> 00:44:12,417
l'm cold.

545
00:44:12,792 --> 00:44:14,692
Your face is so hot, how
can you be cold?

546
00:44:15,795 --> 00:44:17,888
Wouldn't this be faster?

547
00:44:18,063 --> 00:44:19,360
Not fast enough. Faster
would be better.

548
00:44:19,665 --> 00:44:22,065
Faster?!... OK.

549
00:44:28,207 --> 00:44:29,504
Elder...

550
00:44:33,045 --> 00:44:34,342
Elder said he was cold.

551
00:44:35,114 --> 00:44:36,103
Cold?

552
00:44:37,516 --> 00:44:39,416
Elder, you're overly
exerting yourself.

553
00:44:49,161 --> 00:44:51,459
Have you seen Miss Windy?

554
00:44:51,831 --> 00:44:53,321
No, l'm looking for her too.

555
00:44:54,233 --> 00:44:55,427
Where did she go?

556
00:44:59,038 --> 00:45:00,335
There's noise coming from upstairs.
Let's go up for a look.

557
00:45:19,558 --> 00:45:20,650
Don't go up there.

558
00:45:23,429 --> 00:45:24,726
Strange! Nobody up here.

559
00:45:28,868 --> 00:45:30,460
Maybe it's next door.
Let's go over and look.

560
00:45:43,916 --> 00:45:45,213
What are you doing?

561
00:45:45,317 --> 00:45:47,512
Sister, Elder came back to
find me...us.

562
00:45:48,020 --> 00:45:50,511
Why are your clothes so
dishevelled?

563
00:45:52,458 --> 00:45:53,755
Don't be so impolite in
the future.

564
00:45:59,698 --> 00:46:01,598
Miss Windy, this villa is
haunted.

565
00:46:02,501 --> 00:46:03,991
Do we still have to pretend
to be ghosts?

566
00:46:04,470 --> 00:46:06,563
No matter what, we must wait
here for father.

567
00:46:06,972 --> 00:46:08,462
We mustn't leave.

568
00:46:09,875 --> 00:46:10,864
ln this moment of danger,

569
00:46:11,010 --> 00:46:12,409
we must thrust out our
chests and be fearless.

570
00:46:12,578 --> 00:46:14,569
We must be utterly devoted
to our cause.

571
00:46:17,483 --> 00:46:19,383
Elder, let's go in.

572
00:46:22,488 --> 00:46:23,284
Elder!

573
00:46:23,422 --> 00:46:24,616
Your clothes are
torn in the back.

574
00:46:45,911 --> 00:46:47,503
How do you write the
''freeze'' incantation?

575
00:46:54,186 --> 00:46:57,587
l didn't spy on him.l didn't
even know he was outside.

576
00:46:58,490 --> 00:47:00,788
Better tie your heart down.

577
00:47:00,993 --> 00:47:02,483
Otherwise, it might fly away

578
00:47:03,128 --> 00:47:04,117
lf l could tie it down, l would!

579
00:47:18,844 --> 00:47:20,835
This is how you do it...

580
00:47:30,255 --> 00:47:31,347
lt works!

581
00:47:36,829 --> 00:47:38,228
This is the ''freeze''
incantation.

582
00:47:38,397 --> 00:47:41,093
lf you see that monster, do
this and he'll freeze in his tracks.

583
00:47:41,266 --> 00:47:42,062
Like this?

584
00:47:42,234 --> 00:47:44,031
Don't do it haphazardly.This
spell is hard to reverse.

585
00:47:44,136 --> 00:47:45,831
Give me your hand.
Yes!

586
00:47:58,217 --> 00:47:59,206
Sister, what's that sound?

587
00:48:09,228 --> 00:48:13,130
lt's coming from up there.
Windy!

588
00:48:14,633 --> 00:48:16,430
Windy, give me your hand.

589
00:48:16,802 --> 00:48:18,394
Elder, shouldn't you be
calling me Sian?

590
00:48:18,570 --> 00:48:20,265
Whether l call you Sian or
Windy, there's no need to be bashful.

591
00:48:20,806 --> 00:48:22,603
l'll never reveal what
happened just now.

592
00:48:23,542 --> 00:48:24,941
l was really anxious on
your behalf.

593
00:48:25,778 --> 00:48:28,975
Actually, l kissed you
because l couldn't control myself.

594
00:48:29,148 --> 00:48:30,342
Fortunately you made a
quick get-away.

595
00:48:30,749 --> 00:48:32,444
Otherwise, if Moon had seen
you undressed and with me...

596
00:48:32,951 --> 00:48:35,146
it would be hard to explain,
even if l were Elder Chu.

597
00:48:35,988 --> 00:48:37,387
Give me your hand.

598
00:48:38,090 --> 00:48:39,182
Moon?!

599
00:48:39,491 --> 00:48:41,982
Moon, what are you doing here?

600
00:48:43,595 --> 00:48:44,687
l was looking for you.

601
00:48:44,830 --> 00:48:45,819
Don't bother explaining.

602
00:48:46,498 --> 00:48:47,795
Moon!

603
00:48:48,100 --> 00:48:50,500
No, Windy! Give me your hand

604
00:48:50,803 --> 00:48:53,795
We're not fated for each other.
l'm betrothed to Lord Ma's son.

605
00:48:54,740 --> 00:48:56,037
You're betrothed?

606
00:48:56,208 --> 00:48:57,300
We weren't meant for each other.

607
00:48:57,409 --> 00:48:59,809
You should be looking for
Moon, not me.

608
00:49:01,313 --> 00:49:04,805
Windy, one at a time. l'm
after both of you.

609
00:49:13,392 --> 00:49:15,587
Miss Moon, it's getting dark
Give me your hand.

610
00:49:16,562 --> 00:49:17,756
Go to my sister instead.

611
00:49:18,864 --> 00:49:20,957
l'll go to her next. Quick,
give me your hand.

612
00:49:21,333 --> 00:49:22,732
Elder, aren't you the playboy!

613
00:49:22,901 --> 00:49:24,300
You can only choose one of us.

614
00:49:24,536 --> 00:49:25,628
l'm not going to compete
with my sister.

615
00:49:27,406 --> 00:49:30,307
No need to compete. When l
finish with you l'll go to her.

616
00:49:49,495 --> 00:49:52,487
Elder, there is something
l must tell you.

617
00:49:53,932 --> 00:49:55,832
Actually, love is a strange thing.

618
00:49:56,969 --> 00:50:00,166
My heart beats wildly when
l look at you.

619
00:50:01,106 --> 00:50:06,100
l don't even have the
courage to glance at you.

620
00:50:09,515 --> 00:50:12,712
l'm afraid that my heart
would jump right out.

621
00:50:26,331 --> 00:50:27,229
Help!

622
00:50:27,466 --> 00:50:28,558
What's that?

623
00:50:28,667 --> 00:50:30,157
Hurry up! That monster is back.

624
00:50:34,439 --> 00:50:35,337
Go inside and search.

625
00:50:35,440 --> 00:50:36,338
Yes!

626
00:50:37,976 --> 00:50:39,967
lnside there's a huge creature.

627
00:50:40,145 --> 00:50:41,339
l don't know what it is.

628
00:50:50,389 --> 00:50:51,788
Be calm! Use the ''freeze''
incantation.

629
00:50:51,957 --> 00:50:53,049
Together : Freeze!

630
00:50:57,462 --> 00:50:58,759
lt sure does!

631
00:51:06,672 --> 00:51:08,970
We froze it in its tracks.

632
00:51:16,949 --> 00:51:18,143
Everybody, jump up there!

633
00:51:33,398 --> 00:51:34,592
The archery machine!

634
00:51:48,780 --> 00:51:50,372
Be careful!
Elder!

635
00:52:07,866 --> 00:52:09,561
Moon, go and rescue Elder.
l'll lure away that monster.

636
00:52:09,801 --> 00:52:10,699
Yes!

637
00:52:17,509 --> 00:52:18,601
Put out the net.

638
00:52:22,047 --> 00:52:23,344
Your hand...

639
00:52:37,462 --> 00:52:38,554
Let's retreat from here.

640
00:52:45,237 --> 00:52:46,033
See what's going on up ahead

641
00:52:46,104 --> 00:52:47,002
Yes!

642
00:52:50,108 --> 00:52:50,904
Soldiers!

643
00:52:51,076 --> 00:52:52,168
Hu, they've set up an ambush

644
00:52:55,047 --> 00:52:56,344
Windy, Moon?!

645
00:52:56,882 --> 00:52:57,974
lt's father!

646
00:52:58,050 --> 00:52:59,847
Lure the soldiers into the villa.

647
00:52:59,951 --> 00:53:01,248
Use the archery machine to
mow them down!

648
00:53:04,990 --> 00:53:06,184
Trying to get away?

649
00:53:08,160 --> 00:53:09,650
The monster destroyed the
archery machine!

650
00:53:09,828 --> 00:53:10,920
We're surrounded by our toes

651
00:53:12,597 --> 00:53:14,497
Let me out!

652
00:53:14,633 --> 00:53:16,032
Right!... Let Elder go!

653
00:53:16,668 --> 00:53:17,760
Elder, what should we do now?

654
00:53:17,903 --> 00:53:18,801
We'll stay on the sidelines.

655
00:53:18,970 --> 00:53:20,767
When the enemy comes in, the
monster will deal with them.

656
00:53:30,015 --> 00:53:32,415
Obviously a fake ghost. Unmask it.

657
00:53:38,490 --> 00:53:39,787
Let's rescue father!
Yes!

658
00:53:50,001 --> 00:53:50,990
You're hopelessly outnumbered.

659
00:54:00,278 --> 00:54:01,472
l'll save you!

660
00:54:04,116 --> 00:54:07,313
Swords are too dangerous!
Let's use our fists.

661
00:54:21,933 --> 00:54:23,833
l told you that swords are
too dangerous!

662
00:54:45,257 --> 00:54:46,849
Father!

663
00:54:47,459 --> 00:54:48,551
Get out of here. Don't worry
about me!

664
00:54:52,330 --> 00:54:53,922
Don't worry about me! Rescue father!

665
00:55:01,039 --> 00:55:02,336
The monster is here!

666
00:55:03,241 --> 00:55:04,936
Abracadabra! Hocus pocus!

667
00:55:08,346 --> 00:55:09,643
Abraoadabra! Hocus pocus!

668
00:55:13,852 --> 00:55:15,149
Windy! Windy!

669
00:55:16,121 --> 00:55:17,110
Possessed by evil spirits?!

670
00:55:17,389 --> 00:55:18,481
Sister!

671
00:55:18,623 --> 00:55:19,419
What happened to Windy?

672
00:55:19,591 --> 00:55:20,387
She's been possessed by
evil spirits.

673
00:55:20,492 --> 00:55:21,288
What should we do?

674
00:55:21,393 --> 00:55:24,294
Still a lot of soldiers
around. Better get inside.

675
00:55:27,999 --> 00:55:28,988
Don't move!

676
00:55:29,601 --> 00:55:31,068
Press down on her!

677
00:55:31,102 --> 00:55:32,592
Sister!

678
00:55:32,838 --> 00:55:34,430
Think of a way to save
my sister.

679
00:55:34,840 --> 00:55:36,239
She's possessed by the evil spirits.

680
00:55:36,441 --> 00:55:38,033
She could turn into a giant
monster at any moment.

681
00:55:38,510 --> 00:55:40,000
lt's your fault, you traitor.

682
00:55:40,212 --> 00:55:41,110
l'll kill you!

683
00:55:41,947 --> 00:55:43,437
Wait! His troops are still out there.

684
00:55:43,615 --> 00:55:45,310
We must keep him as a hostage.

685
00:55:48,019 --> 00:55:50,214
She's turning into a corpse
monster!

686
00:55:51,423 --> 00:55:52,219
Sister!

687
00:55:52,324 --> 00:55:53,814
We must kill her immediately

688
00:55:53,992 --> 00:55:54,788
Otherwise she'll turn into a monster.

689
00:55:54,893 --> 00:55:56,087
You can't kill her!

690
00:55:56,761 --> 00:55:58,058
Are you a good person or evil?

691
00:55:58,263 --> 00:55:59,560
You won't kill Hu, but
you'll kill my sister.

692
00:55:59,865 --> 00:56:00,763
Kill Hu!

693
00:56:02,300 --> 00:56:03,790
No matter how many you kill here,
you still won't save the kingdom.

694
00:56:04,069 --> 00:56:07,561
The emperor has no idea of
the suffering of his people.

695
00:56:08,106 --> 00:56:10,097
Take my head to the emperor.
Maybe it will move him.

696
00:56:10,308 --> 00:56:13,402
He'll be convinced of our
sincerity and loyalty.

697
00:56:13,578 --> 00:56:16,172
Father, if you die we'll
have no one to lead us.

698
00:56:16,448 --> 00:56:17,642
Take my head instead.

699
00:56:17,916 --> 00:56:19,816
No! Take our heads.

700
00:56:20,318 --> 00:56:22,115
Bastards! What good is it to
cut off your heads?

701
00:56:22,721 --> 00:56:24,018
Who are you, ordering people
about?!

702
00:56:24,322 --> 00:56:26,517
l am the learned and
brilliant Elder Chu!

703
00:56:27,592 --> 00:56:29,184
The learned and brilliant
Elder Chu.

704
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:37,195
Please guide us.

705
00:56:37,702 --> 00:56:39,192
None of you are permitted to die.

706
00:56:39,304 --> 00:56:40,100
Please explain!

707
00:56:40,205 --> 00:56:41,103
Explain?!

708
00:56:41,373 --> 00:56:43,068
Your severed heads will mean
nothing to the emperor.

709
00:56:43,208 --> 00:56:44,607
You'll have died in vain.
Need l explain more?

710
00:56:44,743 --> 00:56:45,835
Stupid pigs!

711
00:56:47,012 --> 00:56:48,604
What about her?

712
00:57:01,560 --> 00:57:05,553
To exorcise her, she needs
a dose of ''yang'' energy.

713
00:57:05,897 --> 00:57:06,989
l am not powerful enough.

714
00:57:07,132 --> 00:57:09,430
We better do something soon
or it will be too late.

715
00:57:09,668 --> 00:57:10,760
What can we do?

716
00:57:10,835 --> 00:57:12,234
Try this magic charm. lt may
or may not work.

717
00:57:12,304 --> 00:57:13,601
Hurry up and pull Miss Windy down.

718
00:57:13,672 --> 00:57:14,570
OK.

719
00:57:28,520 --> 00:57:29,612
l order the evil spirits to
be exercised.

720
00:57:44,436 --> 00:57:45,528
How did this happen?

721
00:57:50,342 --> 00:57:51,331
l've forced the evil spirit from her.

722
00:57:51,476 --> 00:57:53,467
lf she gets a quick dose of ''yang''
energy, there will be a gleam of hope.

723
00:57:53,645 --> 00:57:54,839
Hurry up.

724
00:57:54,980 --> 00:57:56,072
Hurry!

725
00:57:56,348 --> 00:57:58,339
l'm a monk. l must not get
too close to women.

726
00:57:58,683 --> 00:58:00,674
Don't be afraid of her ugliness.

727
00:58:00,952 --> 00:58:01,748
How do we give her ''yang'' energy?

728
00:58:01,853 --> 00:58:03,047
With your mouth, of course.

729
00:58:03,121 --> 00:58:04,019
Mouth?

730
00:58:04,155 --> 00:58:05,247
What then? Your ears?

731
00:58:05,790 --> 00:58:06,882
Send me to her.

732
00:58:07,425 --> 00:58:09,723
Abracadabra! Hocus pocus!

733
00:59:02,647 --> 00:59:03,739
Sister!

734
00:59:11,523 --> 00:59:13,218
A real man is afraid of nothing.

735
00:59:38,283 --> 00:59:41,684
Lord, a golden-robed priest
is on his way here.

736
00:59:43,488 --> 00:59:44,682
A golden-robed priest?

737
01:00:02,607 --> 01:00:03,699
Put your swords down!

738
01:00:06,945 --> 01:00:10,039
Not enough! More!

739
01:00:12,050 --> 01:00:13,244
Lower your swords!

740
01:00:13,885 --> 01:00:14,783
Put all your swords down!

741
01:00:20,425 --> 01:00:23,121
There are evildoers behind
every country's downfall.

742
01:00:23,628 --> 01:00:25,721
Take my head and collect
your reward.

743
01:00:34,105 --> 01:00:36,403
The way that you look death
calmly in the face,

744
01:00:36,708 --> 01:00:38,005
proves that you are loyal to
our country.

745
01:00:40,245 --> 01:00:41,735
Even though our political
views are different,

746
01:00:42,647 --> 01:00:44,638
l'm still willing to help you.

747
01:00:45,850 --> 01:00:49,047
The golden-robed Taoist
outside is the High Priest.

748
01:00:49,888 --> 01:00:50,980
The High Priest?

749
01:00:51,222 --> 01:00:53,315
All the rites and rituals in
the palace...

750
01:00:54,058 --> 01:00:56,151
the emperor consults him
for guidance.

751
01:00:56,361 --> 01:00:58,955
lf he speaks on your behalf,
justice will triumph.

752
01:01:00,465 --> 01:01:01,557
Father!

753
01:01:02,967 --> 01:01:07,461
Lord Fu, if you trust me,
let me go to him.

754
01:01:08,439 --> 01:01:09,633
l'll explain the true situation.

755
01:01:16,047 --> 01:01:17,446
Father, he might betray you!

756
01:01:17,982 --> 01:01:19,973
He could have killed me had
he wanted to.

757
01:01:25,323 --> 01:01:26,722
Still not awake?!

758
01:01:28,526 --> 01:01:30,824
Enough! l'm going to puke.

759
01:01:32,964 --> 01:01:34,454
Elder!

760
01:02:07,298 --> 01:02:09,198
l am here to pay my respects
to the high priest.

761
01:02:09,634 --> 01:02:12,228
Lord Fu is not a traitor.

762
01:02:12,437 --> 01:02:14,530
He is a loyal subject, a patriot.

763
01:02:15,006 --> 01:02:16,303
l hope that you will uphold justice.

764
01:02:17,475 --> 01:02:20,967
There are many who cannot
tell between good and evil.

765
01:02:21,679 --> 01:02:23,579
They do not know the
hardships of the imperial court.

766
01:02:23,948 --> 01:02:26,644
The purpose of my journey
is to pacify the people.

767
01:02:27,151 --> 01:02:31,952
l'll intercede at court on
behalf of these loyal subjects.

768
01:02:32,423 --> 01:02:33,481
Amen! Amen!

769
01:02:33,524 --> 01:02:34,513
Thank you, High Priest!

770
01:02:56,781 --> 01:02:58,271
How are you, Autumn?

771
01:03:02,787 --> 01:03:05,278
Women are very tempting.
lf l didn't exercise self-control...

772
01:03:06,057 --> 01:03:07,547
my energy would have been dissipated.

773
01:03:11,796 --> 01:03:14,993
Hu is treacherous and disrupts
the High Priest's harmony.

774
01:03:15,199 --> 01:03:16,188
Please stay here.

775
01:03:40,224 --> 01:03:43,216
The convict Lord Fu is here
to see the High Priest.

776
01:03:43,561 --> 01:03:45,051
l pay my respects to the High Priest.

777
01:03:45,330 --> 01:03:48,925
Amen! Amen! You have a
murderous air about you.

778
01:03:49,067 --> 01:03:52,264
Put down your weapons.

779
01:03:52,837 --> 01:03:55,635
l've been framed, but l am
concerned about our nation.

780
01:03:56,007 --> 01:04:00,603
You're so merciful.Guide the
emperor to save the nation.

781
01:04:01,112 --> 01:04:04,104
Life is chaotic.

782
01:04:04,349 --> 01:04:07,750
Mistakes can always be corrected.

783
01:04:44,489 --> 01:04:48,983
ln my former life l was evil
so l must do good in this life.

784
01:04:52,964 --> 01:04:56,263
Release my soul from purgatory.

785
01:04:56,968 --> 01:04:58,663
Release my soul from purgatory.

786
01:05:12,517 --> 01:05:13,609
Evil chanting?!

787
01:05:16,054 --> 01:05:17,146
Don't be tricked!

788
01:05:18,222 --> 01:05:19,211
Sit down!

789
01:05:21,392 --> 01:05:23,087
His mercy is false! Don't be
tricked by his devilish voice!

790
01:05:25,463 --> 01:05:27,658
Abracadabra! Freeze!

791
01:05:34,405 --> 01:05:35,497
l order the evil spirits to
be exercised!

792
01:05:49,053 --> 01:05:52,955
l am the absoulute Buddha.

793
01:05:54,225 --> 01:05:55,920
What kind of evil spirit
are you!

794
01:05:56,427 --> 01:05:59,225
Even before Buddha you
refuse to reveal your true appearance!

795
01:05:59,931 --> 01:06:02,126
The spirit of evil?!
l am what l look like!

796
01:06:02,366 --> 01:06:04,561
l don't believe you are Buddha!

797
01:06:05,002 --> 01:06:06,094
Let's go over and see if
you're real or false.

798
01:06:06,237 --> 01:06:07,329
Don't!

799
01:06:18,049 --> 01:06:21,541
Abracadabra! Hocus pocus!

800
01:06:39,137 --> 01:06:39,933
Elder!

801
01:06:40,104 --> 01:06:41,298
The bastard Hu betrayed us.

802
01:06:41,906 --> 01:06:43,305
l'll take care of things here.
Leave quickly!

803
01:06:43,541 --> 01:06:47,136
Abracadabra! Hocus pocus!
The universe revolves.

804
01:06:53,584 --> 01:06:55,484
May Buddha be in your heart.

805
01:06:55,686 --> 01:06:57,881
l knew he was false,
but couldn't conquer him.

806
01:06:59,423 --> 01:07:00,617
l failed!

807
01:07:02,660 --> 01:07:04,651
l can't perform my magic
with you here.

808
01:07:05,129 --> 01:07:07,120
l'll open a tunnel in the
earth for you. Hurry!

809
01:07:14,438 --> 01:07:15,427
Autumn!

810
01:07:15,573 --> 01:07:17,564
Hurry up!

811
01:07:18,142 --> 01:07:19,336
l can't hold out.

812
01:07:20,244 --> 01:07:21,336
Hurry!

813
01:07:21,646 --> 01:07:24,740
Abracadabra! Hurry!

814
01:07:33,791 --> 01:07:34,883
Father!

815
01:07:46,671 --> 01:07:49,162
They've escaped for now but
l'll get them in the end.

816
01:07:49,574 --> 01:07:51,064
Guard the three we've captured!

817
01:07:51,442 --> 01:07:52,534
Yes!

818
01:08:00,618 --> 01:08:01,915
What about Lord Fu?

819
01:08:02,320 --> 01:08:04,117
They have admitted their errors.
They have departed.

820
01:08:04,589 --> 01:08:06,682
People should acknowledge
the immensity of the universe.

821
01:08:06,958 --> 01:08:08,050
l just heard a fight going on.

822
01:08:08,693 --> 01:08:11,594
Your ears aren't clean!

823
01:08:11,762 --> 01:08:16,165
Vacate your mind to attain
perfect peace of mind.

824
01:09:13,724 --> 01:09:14,816
l'm very cold.

825
01:09:48,626 --> 01:09:51,322
Sian!

826
01:09:58,502 --> 01:09:59,992
Don't leave me!

827
01:10:13,217 --> 01:10:14,514
Sian!

828
01:10:20,725 --> 01:10:21,919
Don't be reincarnated so soon.

829
01:10:23,661 --> 01:10:25,060
lt's too hard to be mortal now.

830
01:10:26,063 --> 01:10:27,462
You're so good to Sian.

831
01:10:28,566 --> 01:10:30,659
l never realized how much
you missed her!

832
01:10:31,369 --> 01:10:33,769
l never realized how much
you missed her!

833
01:11:35,866 --> 01:11:37,959
Frost fills the sky over
10 Mile Lake.

834
01:11:38,469 --> 01:11:40,960
Silken threads anxoius of youth.

835
01:11:43,107 --> 01:11:46,008
Looking at the moon and
feeling lonely.

836
01:11:46,377 --> 01:11:54,375
Envious of lovers, not of
immortality.

837
01:12:02,827 --> 01:12:04,124
Sian!

838
01:12:11,936 --> 01:12:13,733
Sian, what are you doing here?

839
01:12:13,971 --> 01:12:15,962
Hide! You can't let the sun
shine on you!

840
01:12:16,240 --> 01:12:17,639
lf the sun shines on you,
your soul will be scattered.

841
01:12:17,775 --> 01:12:19,970
You would never be reincarnated!

842
01:12:21,078 --> 01:12:23,569
Why don't you listen to me? Sian!

843
01:12:29,386 --> 01:12:31,081
Oh, it's you! l'm sorry.

844
01:12:31,388 --> 01:12:32,787
Once again l've made a mistake.

845
01:12:34,658 --> 01:12:35,750
l mistook you for she.

846
01:12:40,598 --> 01:12:42,088
So there really is someone
named Sian!

847
01:12:42,933 --> 01:12:44,127
ls she the one in the painting?

848
01:12:45,336 --> 01:12:46,530
Do you miss her very much?

849
01:12:47,738 --> 01:12:49,535
She's already dead and buried.

850
01:12:50,274 --> 01:12:51,866
We'll never meet again.

851
01:12:55,546 --> 01:12:58,447
lf you want, you can
call me Sian for now.

852
01:12:58,983 --> 01:13:00,075
For now?

853
01:13:04,154 --> 01:13:07,749
l understand.
You're betrothed to another.

854
01:13:09,560 --> 01:13:10,959
When l knew Sian,

855
01:13:11,128 --> 01:13:13,119
she was also betrothed to
somebody else.

856
01:13:13,964 --> 01:13:15,158
lt's beyond my control.

857
01:13:17,434 --> 01:13:19,629
Sian said exactly the same thing.

858
01:13:27,278 --> 01:13:29,769
You are morial; she's a ghost

859
01:13:30,981 --> 01:13:32,278
But you're both exactly the same.

860
01:13:36,754 --> 01:13:38,051
Are we very much alike?

861
01:13:39,523 --> 01:13:40,820
Too much so.

862
01:13:41,292 --> 01:13:42,884
You gave me false hope.

863
01:13:44,328 --> 01:13:46,319
Anyway, false hope is
better than none.

864
01:13:49,833 --> 01:13:50,925
Excuse me!

865
01:13:53,671 --> 01:13:55,866
Here's your tea.

866
01:13:56,473 --> 01:13:57,770
Your meal will be served presently.

867
01:13:58,242 --> 01:13:59,641
Please make yourselves at home.

868
01:14:04,014 --> 01:14:06,312
l've seen that man before. He's...

869
01:14:07,084 --> 01:14:12,078
The tea is poisoned!
This inn is run by thieves!

870
01:14:12,222 --> 01:14:12,916
Really!

871
01:14:12,990 --> 01:14:14,082
ls the water boiling?

872
01:14:14,491 --> 01:14:15,583
The blade sharpened?

873
01:14:15,759 --> 01:14:16,953
Everything's ready.

874
01:14:17,261 --> 01:14:18,159
Put the man in the cauldron
immediately.

875
01:14:18,329 --> 01:14:20,923
Save the woman for tonight,
to warm our cold beds.

876
01:14:21,999 --> 01:14:23,193
Kill!

877
01:14:23,734 --> 01:14:25,429
Slice them up good!

878
01:14:25,569 --> 01:14:31,974
Right on!

879
01:14:33,544 --> 01:14:36,138
Stop!

880
01:14:39,650 --> 01:14:41,845
Watch where you're stabbing!

881
01:14:44,588 --> 01:14:46,385
They escaped through the window.

882
01:14:59,236 --> 01:15:00,726
lt's dangerous here.
This is no way to escape!

883
01:15:04,408 --> 01:15:05,500
Better jump into the tree and hide.

884
01:15:07,411 --> 01:15:09,504
l still haven't recovered.
No energy to jump.

885
01:15:11,615 --> 01:15:13,412
Don't worry about me. Run!

886
01:15:13,550 --> 01:15:15,450
No, l won't leave you.

887
01:15:18,455 --> 01:15:19,945
This time there's no escape!

888
01:15:20,324 --> 01:15:21,916
l never thought we'd die here.

889
01:15:21,992 --> 01:15:23,983
Elder, it's our fault for
getting you involved.

890
01:15:25,529 --> 01:15:26,723
l'm not Elder Chu.

891
01:15:27,131 --> 01:15:28,928
l'm just a poor scholar.

892
01:15:30,134 --> 01:15:31,226
No matter who you are...

893
01:15:31,568 --> 01:15:33,763
l feel fortunate to die
with the one l love.

894
01:15:39,276 --> 01:15:40,470
We'll never be parted again.

895
01:15:46,950 --> 01:15:49,350
We'll never be parted again.
Hold me!

896
01:15:53,190 --> 01:15:56,682
Let me be on the outside so
that the wolf eats me first.

897
01:15:58,729 --> 01:15:59,718
You're wonderful.

898
01:16:03,200 --> 01:16:04,098
So are you.

899
01:16:04,968 --> 01:16:06,265
lf we could be like this
forever, it would be great.

900
01:16:40,237 --> 01:16:43,729
Orchid Monastery!

901
01:16:43,941 --> 01:16:44,839
Orchid Monastery!

902
01:16:45,042 --> 01:16:46,134
What's the Orchid Monastery?

903
01:16:50,981 --> 01:16:52,278
How could l have forgotten
about Yan?

904
01:16:52,483 --> 01:16:53,381
Who is he?

905
01:16:53,917 --> 01:16:55,817
The bearded man in the Orchid
Monastery. A wizard in the occult.

906
01:16:56,286 --> 01:16:58,186
lf we find him, we can deal
with the High Priest.

907
01:17:10,834 --> 01:17:12,324
lsn't the High Priest
returning to the capital city?

908
01:17:13,470 --> 01:17:14,767
Why go to his palace?

909
01:17:15,572 --> 01:17:18,370
He needs a tranquil place
to meditate.

910
01:17:24,581 --> 01:17:27,072
Only holy people may enter
this sacred place. Stay where you are.

911
01:17:49,506 --> 01:17:51,098
This is the hour of the eclipse.

912
01:17:55,445 --> 01:18:00,348
My body is changing against
my wish.

913
01:18:18,669 --> 01:18:20,762
Why are all the officials of
the imperial court here?

914
01:18:29,213 --> 01:18:32,614
Lord Chiang! Lord Yang! Lord Lee!

915
01:18:34,284 --> 01:18:36,878
l was escorting Lord Fu back
to the capital...

916
01:18:37,054 --> 01:18:39,045
But couldn't complete my
mission. Allow me to explain

917
01:18:42,526 --> 01:18:44,619
Lord Chiang!

918
01:18:47,331 --> 01:18:48,320
A hollow shell?

919
01:18:48,832 --> 01:18:52,324
Lord Yang is a hollow shell, too?

920
01:18:52,870 --> 01:18:54,963
What kind of a place is this?
Are you demons?

921
01:18:55,172 --> 01:18:57,470
What did you do with the
flesh and blood of these officials?

922
01:19:03,080 --> 01:19:04,980
You demons, come out and
face me!

923
01:19:10,420 --> 01:19:11,910
Why did you do with the flesh and
blood of these officials?

924
01:19:12,089 --> 01:19:12,987
What evil intentions do you
harbour?

925
01:19:15,492 --> 01:19:16,584
Are they all hollow shells?!

926
01:19:17,861 --> 01:19:20,659
l'm going to destroy all of
you evil monks.

927
01:19:28,505 --> 01:19:29,995
Strange, where have they hidden?

928
01:19:42,252 --> 01:19:45,551
Autumn? Moon? Lord Fu?

929
01:19:46,590 --> 01:19:48,581
Lord Fu!

930
01:19:51,128 --> 01:19:52,925
What happened?
Where are the others?

931
01:19:54,364 --> 01:19:56,264
l was wrong to believe you!
You've caused so much harm!

932
01:19:56,500 --> 01:19:57,296
What other plots do you have
up your sleave?

933
01:19:57,401 --> 01:19:59,596
We were tricked.
The High Priest is a demon!

934
01:19:59,937 --> 01:20:01,837
He turned many officials
into walking corpses.

935
01:20:02,606 --> 01:20:04,096
We must report this to the emperor.

936
01:20:04,308 --> 01:20:05,707
Otherwise, the kingdom will
be beyond redemption.

937
01:20:06,443 --> 01:20:07,740
Oh, he's the one who
instigated this calamity!

938
01:20:07,945 --> 01:20:09,242
No wonder the court is in
upheaval.

939
01:20:09,546 --> 01:20:10,945
We must hurry to rescue the others.
We can talk later.

940
01:20:15,652 --> 01:20:17,347
Moon!

941
01:20:24,661 --> 01:20:25,753
Autumn!

942
01:20:26,363 --> 01:20:29,560
There are demons in the court, so l must
get involved in affairs of state

943
01:20:29,733 --> 01:20:30,722
Everyone must do his bit.

944
01:20:32,402 --> 01:20:33,596
Hurry! There's danger everywhere.

945
01:20:33,737 --> 01:20:34,829
Let's get past this hurdle first.

946
01:20:36,640 --> 01:20:37,629
These demonic monks have
great magical powers.

947
01:20:37,808 --> 01:20:39,400
Once he's awake we won't be
able to escape, so hurry!

948
01:20:41,378 --> 01:20:42,777
Autumn, get out of here!
Don't fight anymore!

949
01:20:45,015 --> 01:20:45,811
This is a scene of desolation.

950
01:20:45,916 --> 01:20:47,213
Lord, ride my horse.

951
01:20:50,821 --> 01:20:51,719
More chanting!

952
01:20:51,855 --> 01:20:53,152
l'll use my powers to
help you concentrate.

953
01:20:55,258 --> 01:20:56,953
Come back, Hu.
You'll never beat him.

954
01:22:08,365 --> 01:22:11,061
Put down your butchers' knives.
Bow before Buddha!

955
01:22:14,871 --> 01:22:16,771
Hu, don't sacrifice yourself in vain!

956
01:22:18,408 --> 01:22:20,000
l mistakenly trusted these demons
and slaughtered righteous officials.

957
01:22:20,544 --> 01:22:22,637
To atone for my sins,
l'll fight him to the death.

958
01:22:25,082 --> 01:22:26,276
Don't!

959
01:22:26,550 --> 01:22:28,541
l'm headed for hell anyway.

960
01:22:32,923 --> 01:22:34,117
Hu!

961
01:22:37,594 --> 01:22:39,687
Yan, why does the wind
suddenly blow so violently?

962
01:22:40,163 --> 01:22:41,357
lt's hard to tell which
direction is which.

963
01:22:42,432 --> 01:22:43,729
Yan, what should we do?

964
01:22:44,000 --> 01:22:47,094
Evil spirits pervade this road.
Our lives hang by a clender thread.

965
01:22:47,304 --> 01:22:48,601
We mustn't stop. Follow me!

966
01:22:58,415 --> 01:23:00,508
Oh, boundless heaven and earth!
Help me!

967
01:23:09,226 --> 01:23:13,526
Recite the scriptures with
me! Prajna paramita...

968
01:23:15,532 --> 01:23:18,831
Prajna paramita...

969
01:23:24,007 --> 01:23:25,099
The Diamond Sutra incantation?

970
01:23:26,376 --> 01:23:27,468
Prajna paramita...

971
01:23:31,848 --> 01:23:34,646
lgnoramus, behaving so
boorishly in front of me!

972
01:23:35,485 --> 01:23:36,782
Prajna paramite...

973
01:23:39,523 --> 01:23:41,320
Ning, Windy...get out of the way!

974
01:23:41,625 --> 01:23:43,115
Oh, boundless heaven and earth.
Help me!

975
01:23:49,799 --> 01:23:54,395
Buddha is present!

976
01:23:59,509 --> 01:24:01,704
lf you dare to impersonate Buddha,
what would you not dare to do?

977
01:24:02,145 --> 01:24:05,342
You think you can hoodwink
the people forever?

978
01:24:06,216 --> 01:24:09,014
l'm going to let everyone
know what you really are!

979
01:24:09,686 --> 01:24:12,086
The masses love to worship
their idols.

980
01:24:12,289 --> 01:24:14,689
Why set yourself against the people?

981
01:24:15,792 --> 01:24:18,590
lt's their ignorance that
has allowed you to succeed.

982
01:24:18,895 --> 01:24:20,192
l'll never let them worship
demons like you.

983
01:24:20,463 --> 01:24:21,259
You'll never decieve the
people again!

984
01:24:21,831 --> 01:24:25,232
lf you refuse to follow my
shining beacon...

985
01:24:25,669 --> 01:24:27,364
you will be destroyed!

986
01:24:28,271 --> 01:24:32,571
What crap! Look out!

987
01:24:38,682 --> 01:24:40,274
Justine for all!

988
01:24:48,725 --> 01:24:49,817
Swords are part of the infinite!

989
01:24:56,733 --> 01:24:58,325
We've only destroyed the
false cuter body.

990
01:24:58,435 --> 01:24:59,333
He can come back &
attack us at any time.

991
01:24:59,436 --> 01:25:01,028
We must use our swords
to fight back!

992
01:25:01,338 --> 01:25:03,431
Let me introduce myself.
l'm from the Kunlun sect...

993
01:25:03,840 --> 01:25:05,239
At a time like this,
let's not separate into sects.

994
01:25:05,408 --> 01:25:07,501
We're all fighting the same enemy.
Destroy this demon!

995
01:25:07,744 --> 01:25:08,642
Chant with me!

996
01:25:08,979 --> 01:25:11,971
Prajna paramita...

997
01:25:12,115 --> 01:25:18,213
Prajna paramita...

998
01:25:43,113 --> 01:25:44,910
The old demon has stolen into the earth
and broken through our ring of swords.

999
01:25:45,115 --> 01:25:46,605
What should we do?

1000
01:25:46,750 --> 01:25:47,648
Watch!

1001
01:25:50,420 --> 01:25:51,409
What kind of demon?

1002
01:25:51,588 --> 01:25:52,680
Come with me!

1003
01:25:59,329 --> 01:26:00,819
Hold on to me as l fly.

1004
01:26:03,366 --> 01:26:04,355
Ning!

1005
01:26:04,901 --> 01:26:06,095
You pulled my sleave off.

1006
01:26:12,509 --> 01:26:13,601
What are you coming back for

1007
01:26:16,046 --> 01:26:17,035
What happened?

1008
01:26:17,947 --> 01:26:19,244
Gone?

1009
01:26:41,204 --> 01:26:42,193
Be careful!

1010
01:26:50,547 --> 01:26:52,538
Moon, look after your father
l'll help Yan.

1011
01:26:53,316 --> 01:26:54,613
Autumn, be careful!

1012
01:26:55,785 --> 01:26:56,774
The demon's actually a
giant centipede!

1013
01:26:56,920 --> 01:26:59,616
That worm can never be a dragon.

1014
01:26:59,823 --> 01:27:00,721
Elder!

1015
01:27:09,799 --> 01:27:11,790
l've never had to deal with
such a giant creature.

1016
01:27:12,068 --> 01:27:12,966
What should we do now?

1017
01:27:13,036 --> 01:27:14,628
Pierce the crown of its head

1018
01:27:24,581 --> 01:27:25,479
Ning!

1019
01:27:35,925 --> 01:27:36,914
Windy!

1020
01:27:45,101 --> 01:27:46,898
The flying sword!

1021
01:28:26,743 --> 01:28:27,937
Prajna paramita!

1022
01:28:30,947 --> 01:28:32,039
Exercise the demons!

1023
01:28:36,386 --> 01:28:38,377
Oh, boundless heaven and
earth. Help me!

1024
01:28:47,330 --> 01:28:48,126
Elder!

1025
01:28:48,298 --> 01:28:49,196
Autumn!

1026
01:28:51,034 --> 01:28:52,433
Two heads are better than one.

1027
01:28:52,602 --> 01:28:54,593
Abracadabra. Hocus pocus.

1028
01:29:02,312 --> 01:29:03,802
Hocus pocus.

1029
01:29:36,913 --> 01:29:38,710
l've been in the Orchid
Monastery for so long...

1030
01:29:38,848 --> 01:29:41,840
l didn't know the world was
so full of devils and demons

1031
01:29:42,151 --> 01:29:43,448
lt's hard to separate the
living from the dead.

1032
01:29:43,720 --> 01:29:45,517
The world is in chaos.

1033
01:29:46,322 --> 01:29:47,619
lt's a good thing you hid in
the Orchid Monastery.

1034
01:29:47,924 --> 01:29:49,824
Otherwise l might never
have found you.

1035
01:29:50,727 --> 01:29:51,819
We share the same ideals...

1036
01:29:52,061 --> 01:29:54,052
We should roam this world together
and fight for justice.

1037
01:29:54,264 --> 01:29:55,253
We should work together.

1038
01:29:55,865 --> 01:29:57,059
What are you saying?

1039
01:29:57,133 --> 01:29:58,828
l've always led a solitary existence.

1040
01:29:59,035 --> 01:30:01,936
Last time, l almost died
trying to help you save Sian

1041
01:30:02,105 --> 01:30:04,005
This time, l've helped you
battle the demons...

1042
01:30:04,107 --> 01:30:04,903
and almost lost my life.

1043
01:30:04,974 --> 01:30:06,168
lt's better if we go our own ways.

1044
01:30:06,376 --> 01:30:08,674
When you need my help,
l'll return and save you.

1045
01:30:24,627 --> 01:30:26,026
Be careful, Autumn!

1046
01:30:45,548 --> 01:30:47,948
We're locked in. We must
think of a way to escape.

1047
01:30:48,685 --> 01:30:51,984
You're right! l've really
caused you harm.

1048
01:30:57,293 --> 01:31:00,194
Our bodies are restrained. We can be
saved only if our souls can escape.

1049
01:31:00,730 --> 01:31:02,027
Souls?

1050
01:31:02,098 --> 01:31:05,397
Will we have enough energy
to later let the souls back in?

1051
01:31:06,336 --> 01:31:07,735
This is the only way!

1052
01:31:07,804 --> 01:31:09,601
Chant along with me.

1053
01:31:13,476 --> 01:31:18,573
The spirit of Buddha conquers all!

1054
01:31:19,849 --> 01:31:26,846
Goodness is indestructible.

1055
01:31:34,897 --> 01:31:38,298
Oh, boundless heaven and earth.
Help me!

1056
01:31:39,936 --> 01:31:42,837
Help me!
Hocus pocus!

1057
01:32:09,465 --> 01:32:10,762
Autumn!

1058
01:32:15,471 --> 01:32:17,063
Yan!
Autumn!

1059
01:32:18,241 --> 01:32:19,333
Yan!

1060
01:32:19,742 --> 01:32:20,936
Soul, return!

1061
01:32:26,949 --> 01:32:28,041
My soul can't return to my body!

1062
01:32:29,385 --> 01:32:30,977
Autumn, catch the soul!

1063
01:32:36,926 --> 01:32:39,326
His power isn't strong enough.
l'll help him.

1064
01:32:39,529 --> 01:32:41,019
Prajna paramita...

1065
01:32:42,765 --> 01:32:44,062
l can't catch it.

1066
01:32:44,867 --> 01:32:45,959
Moon!

1067
01:34:29,205 --> 01:34:30,194
What's all the hubub outside

1068
01:34:30,273 --> 01:34:31,570
What hubbub? l don't hear
anything!

1069
01:34:50,092 --> 01:34:51,992
Who's getting married?
Such a large golden pig!

1070
01:34:53,930 --> 01:34:56,023
lt's a gift to Lord Fu from
the emperor.

1071
01:34:57,767 --> 01:34:59,667
Since he exposed the
traitors in the imperial

1072
01:35:00,036 --> 01:35:01,230
court, he performed a great
service for the emperor.

1073
01:35:01,370 --> 01:35:03,861
lt's a wedding gift for Lord
Fu's daughter.

1074
01:35:07,610 --> 01:35:09,009
Moon!

1075
01:35:09,946 --> 01:35:11,436
Moon!

1076
01:35:12,415 --> 01:35:13,712
Ning!

1077
01:35:20,256 --> 01:35:21,655
ls Windy getting...

1078
01:35:22,158 --> 01:35:23,352
Sister is already married.

1079
01:35:23,526 --> 01:35:25,016
Don't cause her any trouble.

1080
01:35:27,363 --> 01:35:28,352
l'm about to start on a journey.

1081
01:35:28,464 --> 01:35:31,262
Give her my best wishes for
a happy marriage.

1082
01:35:34,670 --> 01:35:37,161
l will. Take care of yourself.

1083
01:35:48,184 --> 01:35:49,276
Adieu!

1084
01:36:04,166 --> 01:36:06,259
lt's hard to differentiate
between true and false hopes

1085
01:36:06,802 --> 01:36:09,794
Now l understand why you
stay away from our mortal world.

1086
01:36:10,473 --> 01:36:13,567
Mortals are forgetful.
Good deeds fade like the wind.

1087
01:36:14,010 --> 01:36:16,604
No matter what you've done,
it's soon forgotten.

1088
01:36:17,546 --> 01:36:19,446
ls forgetting good or bad?

1089
01:36:19,849 --> 01:36:21,544
Should we have hopes?

1090
01:36:35,097 --> 01:36:36,587
You said you'd cherish no
hopes!

1091
01:36:37,566 --> 01:36:39,363
Sister, don't hesitate!
Go to him!

1092
01:36:47,576 --> 01:36:48,372
Windy?!

1093
01:36:48,477 --> 01:36:49,375
Ning!

1094
01:36:50,079 --> 01:36:52,479
Let's go, hurry!

1095
01:36:53,983 --> 01:36:54,881
You go back.

1096
01:36:54,984 --> 01:36:57,282
Farewell!
Take care!

1097
01:36:58,587 --> 01:36:59,576
Let's go!

1098
01:37:06,629 --> 01:37:09,325
The path of life

1099
01:37:09,899 --> 01:37:13,391
Are dreams, like the length of the path

1100
01:37:14,203 --> 01:37:17,001
The storm on the way

1101
01:37:17,173 --> 01:37:21,075
Pass by as you go along

1102
01:37:22,044 --> 01:37:25,138
ln the world

1103
01:37:25,348 --> 01:37:28,840
How many ways can one dream?

1104
01:37:29,585 --> 01:37:34,181
Looking for dream-like love

1105
01:37:34,590 --> 01:37:38,390
And the path goes on

1106
01:37:39,695 --> 01:37:42,596
Life is what

1107
01:37:42,865 --> 01:37:46,266
Dreams and desires are made of

1108
01:37:47,169 --> 01:37:49,967
Somewhere in the dream

1109
01:37:50,139 --> 01:37:54,542
There are traces of tears

1110
01:37:55,011 --> 01:37:58,208
Where to go to?

1111
01:37:58,381 --> 01:38:01,873
To find where my heart wants to go

1112
01:38:02,518 --> 01:38:07,217
The wind seems to sign in the dream,

1113
01:38:07,523 --> 01:38:11,516
and the path and l go on.

1114
01:38:16,265 --> 01:38:19,359
The path of living

1115
01:38:19,735 --> 01:38:23,034
The happiness of youth

1116
01:38:24,006 --> 01:38:26,497
The path is full of difficulties

1117
01:38:26,976 --> 01:38:30,673
That no light can be seen

1118
01:38:31,781 --> 01:38:34,875
ln the dust,

1119
01:38:35,151 --> 01:38:38,746
how many ways can one find happiness

1120
01:38:39,355 --> 01:38:43,951
The wind and rain pass like a dream,

1121
01:38:44,427 --> 01:38:49,228
and the path goes on.

